WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.750
Good morning John, it's Sunday, August 3rd,
2014.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:04.750
And I love you.

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:08.510
You're a good brother, you're a good person,
and I'm lucky to have you in my life.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:11.741
I don't know where I'd be without you, or
who I'd be without you.

00:00:11.741 --> 00:00:16.660
You make me a better person, you help me make
better decisions, you've been a good person

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.190
to look up to as a child and as an adult,
and you just have good values.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:24.000
Even thought apparently you told a bunch of
people at LeakyCon that I have a little bit

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.820
of a problem with showering when I was 10,
true.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.030
You could of kept that one to yourself.

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:34.769
If you're confused with why I'm being so unironically
sappy right now, it's because today is Esther

00:00:34.769 --> 00:00:35.769
Day.

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:39.899
In 2010 John asked Esther Earl, a nerdfighter
who helped inspire The Fault in Our Stars,

00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:43.800
what she would like us as a community to do
on her birthday.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.100
She said she wanted it to be a day to celebrate
the kind of love that people have inside of

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.170
families and friendships, not romantic love.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:56.409
John as you put it last year, you said, "It's
a Valentine's Day for the rest of love".

00:00:56.409 --> 00:01:00.170
Because, you know, we're obsessed with romantic
love, and I get that.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:01.170
I understand.

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:05.869
But love is so much more than that, between
parents and children and siblings and friends.

00:01:05.869 --> 00:01:09.979
It's the kind of boring everyday love that
ties the whole world together.

00:01:09.979 --> 00:01:14.250
So on this day, we say "I love you" to the
people who we don't normally say "I love you"

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.250
to.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.860
So, I'm asking, take some time out of your
day to do that thing.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:22.079
It's just, it's a good thing to do, and if
that's not enough for you, it's what Esther

00:01:22.079 --> 00:01:23.079
wants.

00:01:23.079 --> 00:01:24.200
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:28.479
Good morning John, it's August 3rd, 2013,
and I love you-is it?

00:01:28.479 --> 00:01:29.799
It's 2014, yup.

